		<outline text="email about Armistice Day">
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Commenter's name: "/>
			<outline text="Rob"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Email address: "/>
			<outline text="nospam@nospam.com"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Web site: "/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="IP address: "/>
			<outline text="65.208.142.19"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Domain name: "/>
			<outline text="smtp2.hsgt.com"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Commenting on: "/>
			<outline text="http://www.blognewsnetwork.com/members/0000001/2004/11/11.html#a6858"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Adam, I am surprised that someone living in Flanders would not know something about Armistice day, the end of World War 1, when Germany surrendered to the Allies at 1100 on the 11th day of the 11th month of 1918. Here Canada we observe November 11 as Remembrance Day by wearing  a red poppy and often read the famous poem below:  In Flanders Fields By: Lieutenant Colonel John McCrae, MD (1872-1918) Canadian Army IN FLANDERS FIELDS the poppies blow Between the crosses row on row, That mark our place; and in the sky The larks, still bravely singing, fly Scarce heard amid the guns below. We are the Dead. Short days ago We lived, felt dawn, saw sunset glow, Loved and were loved, and now we lie In Flanders fields. Take up our quarrel with the foe: To you from failing hands we throw The torch; be yours to hold it high. If ye break faith with us who die We shall not sleep, though poppies grow In Flanders fields."/>
			</outline>
		<outline text="iPodder Ears">
			<outline text="email from Adam Chernow">
				<outline text="From: 	  Adam Chernow &lt;ac@commanddotcom.com&gt;"/>
				<outline text="Subject: 	iPodder Ear...."/>
				<outline text="Date: 	November 13, 2004 10:00:20 AM CET"/>
				<outline text="To: 	  Adam Curry &lt;adam@curry.com&gt;"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Adam,"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Listening to the show for the past couple of days and you mentioned that"/>
				<outline text="you were getting iPod ear (or something like that) form those damn iPod"/>
				<outline text="headphones.... Well, in addition to whatever the headphones were that you"/>
				<outline text="had on the 11/12 show, I have a recommendation for you.... Studio"/>
				<outline text="headphones.  It sounds crazy, but if you're doing a lot of recording, you"/>
				<outline text="might want to invest in a pair.  I have a great pair made by Sony that I"/>
				<outline text="bought 4 years ago, when I was working at a college radio station.  I"/>
				<outline text="love them!  Hell, I even hooked them up to the iPod on the flight from"/>
				<outline text="Chicago/O'Hare to London/Heathrow (the battery didn't make it all the"/>
				<outline text="way, but I had a Belekin back-up battery adapter).  The other thing I do"/>
				<outline text="is that I don't use the iPod headphones with my iPod, most of the time..."/>
				<outline text="I use headphones that I had to of gotten in the mid-90s for a Discman I"/>
				<outline text="had at that time.  The ear pads are falling off, they're beat to hell,"/>
				<outline text="but they still sound good and they're infinitely more comfortable than"/>
				<outline text="the iPod headphones."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="-Adam Chernow"/>
				<outline text="-- "/>
				<outline text="Adam Chernow"/>
				<outline text="web:    http://www.commanddotcom.com"/>
				<outline text="aim: vbrun400 / yahoo: thecptrgod / icq: 16013022"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Words to think about..."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="&quot;All that matters in a relationship is that you both like"/>
				<outline text="the same pizza toppings&quot;    -Daria"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				</outline>
			<outline text="email from Rene">
				<outline text="From: 	  René Poelen &lt;r.poelen@chello.nl&gt;"/>
				<outline text="Subject: 	Mousefinger make/model?"/>
				<outline text="Date: 	November 12, 2004 7:08:40 PM CET"/>
				<outline text="To: 	  Adam Curry &lt;adam@curry.com&gt;"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Hi Adam,"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="listened to your DSC 11-10-2004 and it was very interesting again..."/>
				<outline text="You mentioned the fingermouse wireless with scrollwheel. Now I 've been trying to find it online but no luck (yet)."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Could you provide the make model?"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Keep up the good stuff and enjopy your move into a new country...."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="till iPod"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="René"/>
				</outline>
			<outline text="email from James">
				<outline text="From: 	  James Invincible &lt;james@theinvincibles.org&gt;"/>
				<outline text="Subject: 	headphones and other thoughts"/>
				<outline text="Date: 	November 11, 2004 8:03:39 PM CET"/>
				<outline text="To: 	  Adam Curry &lt;adam@curry.com&gt;"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Adam,"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="I've been there, and completely understand what you mean about &quot;podcast ear&quot; - I found that when wearing the de facto iPod earbuds that my ears would become sore after time as well.  I went through a bunch of others until I hit upon, IMHO, an awesome set from Sony. Unfortunately, it looks like the model I personally use has been deprecated, but the MDR-ED21LP seems to be in the same form factor. It is lamentable that Sony  has moved away from this design in their newer earbuds, as the new design is pretty uncomfortable."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="I listened to the DSC this morning, and recognized the &quot;Promiscuous Bullet&quot; voices as the two kids whom I sat near at the BloggerCon podCast dinner - If I were to describe meeting Tamas and Stephen, I think it could easily be construed as them being &quot;rockstarish&quot; and &quot;elitist&quot; - I definitely found them to be hipsters...  but I sat back and thought about it first... they were just shy and feeling out of their element.  I really think that you've handled their acidity in a really genuine way, and I appreciate that."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="In other news, we did a split Dawn and Drew show last night, with Dawn recording her channel on our end, and Drew his - then Drew did the merging... I think it sounds pretty good.  It is definitely a technique that could be honed and automated, but I'm working on it."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="That's about all.  Hope that your move is as unobtrusive to your daily life as possible."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Cheers,"/>
				<outline text="James"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="http://www.sonystyle.com/is-bin/INTERSHOP.enfinity/eCS/Store/en/-/USD/SY_DisplayProductInformation-Start?ProductSKU=MDRED21LP&amp;Dept=pa&amp;CategoryName=pa_PADepartmentAccessories_Headphones_Fontopia%2e%2fEarbud"/>
				<outline text="-- "/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="@a=(Lbzjoftt,Inqbujfodf,"/>
				<outline text="Hvcsjt); $b=&quot;Lbssz Wbmm&quot;"/>
				<outline text=";$b =~ y/b-z/a-z/ ; $c ="/>
				<outline text="&quot; Tif &quot;. @a .&quot; hsfbu wj&quot;"/>
				<outline text=".&quot;suvft pg b qsphsbnnfs&quot;"/>
				<outline text=". &quot;:\n&quot;;$c =~y/b-y/a-z/;"/>
				<outline text="print&quot;\n\n$c &quot;;for($i=0;"/>
				<outline text="$i&lt;@a; $i++) { $a[$i] =~"/>
				<outline text="y/b-y/a-z/;if($a[$i]eq$a"/>
				<outline text="[-1]){print&quot;and $a[$i].&quot;"/>
				<outline text=";}else{ print&quot;$a[$i], &quot;;"/>
				<outline text="}}print&quot;\n\t\t--$b\n\n&quot;;"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				</outline>
			<outline text="Stuart Hunter">
				<outline text="From: 	  Stuart Hunter &lt;shuntera@gmail.com&gt;"/>
				<outline text="Subject: 	Headphone Suggestion"/>
				<outline text="Date: 	November 12, 2004 3:09:16 PM CET"/>
				<outline text="To: 	  Adam Curry &lt;adam@curry.com&gt;"/>
				<outline text="Reply-To: 	  Stuart Hunter &lt;shuntera@gmail.com&gt;"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Adam,"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="I had the same problem as you with hurting my ears with earbuds."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="I chose to use the Sony MDR-W08 headphones. Very lightweight, they"/>
				<outline text="just sit slightly inside the ear rather than being stuffed right in"/>
				<outline text="like an earbud."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="Also unlike an earbud thay are easy to remove and leave hanging round"/>
				<outline text="your neck when you do have to communicate with the outside world."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="The sound is not as intense as earbuds - like I said - they aren't"/>
				<outline text="jammed in your ears, but they are just fine for listening to podcasts."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="http://www.circuitcity.com/rpsm/oid/16242/rpem/ccd/productDetailReview.do"/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="And Richer Sounds in the UK are selling them off dirt cheap."/>
				<outline text=""/>
				<outline text="http://www.richersounds.sv01.net/index.php?f=itemdetl.php&amp;p=300081"/>
				</outline>
			</outline>
		<outline text="email from Tony from Oz">
			<outline text="From: 	  ncleknight@hotmail.com"/>
			<outline text="Subject: 	Radio UserLand: Mail from Tony"/>
			<outline text="Date: 	November 12, 2004 4:20:58 PM CET"/>
			<outline text="To: 	  Adam Curry &lt;adam@curry.com&gt;"/>
			<outline text="Cc: 	  ncleknight@hotmail.com"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Tony  [1] sent this email to you through the Radio UserLand [2] community server, re this page [3]. "/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Gday Adam,"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="I work in a call center but christ I won't put my last name in cause I can probably get sacked for that (). I love your podcasts they are raw man they are like getting stoned with your mates and listening to shit you wouldn't normally listen to ( that aside ). "/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="What hardware do you do your podcasts on cause I would like to know ( you probably told people this on podcast 1 ), fark like you are going to tell me."/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="I spend probably 10 hrs outside every weekend in the yard - ( it's Australia ) non rugby league season of course :) man your casts breeze me through thru the weekend... THANKYOU"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Maybe you can pop the question  ( A member of the coalition of the willing ) when Apple Itunes might immigrate to Australia. "/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="I didn't word that right btw, anyway .... Immigrate is that the right word??"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Man anyway I love the show if you get a chance drop a reply. If not who cares but I really like yours and Daves point of view."/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="MCN the beach boys = priceless"/>
			<outline text="Elton John was fitting on that crappy day we had to face four more years of Bush - and I live in OZ"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="Thanks for your time,"/>
			<outline text="Tone"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text=""/>
			<outline text="[1] http://"/>
			<outline text="[2] http://radio.userland.com/"/>
			<outline text="[3] http://radio.weblogs.com/0001014/categories/dailySourceCode/2004/11/03.html"/>
			<outline text=""/>
			</outline>
